This example demonstrates how to configure a schema quota and then observe diskquota soft limit behavior as data is added to the schema. The example assumes that the diskquota processes are configured and running. Create a database named testdb and connect to it. $ createdb testdb
$ psql -d testdb Create the diskquota extension in the database. CREATE EXTENSION diskquota; Create a schema named s1: CREATE SCHEMA s1; Set a 1MB disk quota for the s1 schema. SELECT diskquota.set_schema_quota('s1', '1MB'); Run the following commands to create a table in the s1 schema and insert a small amount of data into it. The schema has no data yet, so it is not on the denylist. SET search_path TO s1;
